  "literature_notes": "All six ledger lines were evaluated. L1/L2/L3 (PMC2213087) describe EGFP inserted after Leu55 (confirmed: seq[55]=L), but this is a truncation construct \u2014 DC-STAMP(1\u201355)\u2013EGFP \u2014 in which EGFP replaces TM2 through TM7; it is not a full-length membrane-anchored protein and therefore does not qualify as a surface tag site. Additionally, residue 55 is the last residue of TM1 (33\u201355), placing the junction at the TM boundary (0 residues from TM), failing the \u22653-residue constraint. L4 (PMC5386838) describes a functional DC-STAMP-GFP fusion that rescued osteoclast cell-cell fusion, but the GFP is C-terminal and the C-terminus (residue 470) is intracellular (390\u2013470); no extracellular residue is named. L5 (PMC5386838) reports surface expression of DC-STAMP constructs but names no tag insertion site. L6 (PMC3304467) describes a large chimeric domain swap (PTHR extracellular domain fused to DC-STAMP), not a short epitope tag insertion, and names no residue. No ledger line supports a short epitope tag tolerated at an extracellular position of full-length, membrane-anchored DC-STAMP. Zero sites is the correct answer.",
